1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,440
Within the evaluated model pool, Web Catalyst improves Qwen's average rank from fourteen

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:08,911
to four, using just six hundred and forty training requests.

3
00:00:08,911 --> 00:00:12,728
It reaches performance comparable to Claude Opus four point seven.

4
00:00:12,728 --> 00:00:17,240
Watch all six models respond to the same three dimensional flight game prompt.

5
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:23,918
Mini games expose what shallow webpage tests can miss: long action sequences, coupled

6
00:00:23,918 --> 00:00:26,772
state transitions, and visual failures that emerge during execution.

7
00:00:26,772 --> 00:00:29,500
They become a demanding training ground for broader capabilities.

8
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:33,492
The contribution is a unified high fidelity learning signal.

9
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:36,373
A game level assessor grounds evaluation in experience.

10
00:00:36,373 --> 00:00:38,258
Visual Anchor calibrates the reward.

11
00:00:38,258 --> 00:00:42,500
Action Trace Credit redistributes learning signals using actual runtime evidence.

12
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:47,253
Each artifact is treated as a state machine executed in a real browser.

13
00:00:47,253 --> 00:00:51,650
Every transition combines before and after screenshots, an action, and execution

14
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:55,223
metadata. Step level judgments feed a trajectory level evaluator.

15
00:00:55,223 --> 00:00:59,950
A producer consumer queue overlaps execution and judgment, making sustained assessment

16
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:00,500
practical.

17
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:05,730
Visual Anchor closes a specific loophole: improving verifiable interactions by

18
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:10,279
simplifying the visual design. It compares the best observed screenshot from each

19
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:12,413
rollout with a high quality reference.

20
00:01:12,413 --> 00:01:16,906
The degradation penalty is one sided: equal or better visuals are not penalized.

21
00:01:16,906 --> 00:01:20,500
The calibrated reward subtracts this penalty from the GUI score.

22
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:25,999
The key attribution insight is to trace successful actions, rather than blame failed

23
00:01:25,999 --> 00:01:28,379
ones whose responsible code may be missing.

24
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:32,973
Browser call stacks identify executed functions, which are mapped back to generated

25
00:01:32,973 --> 00:01:37,622
tokens. The minimum observed call depth defines a decaying coefficient, strongest at

26
00:01:37,622 --> 00:01:40,500
leaf level logic and zero outside successful traces.

27
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,355
Credit modulation respects the sign of the page advantage.

28
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:48,863
Successful code receives stronger positive updates on good samples, and weaker negative

29
00:01:48,863 --> 00:01:51,505
updates on poor samples, relative to untraced code.

30
00:01:51,505 --> 00:01:53,733
Normalization preserves the mean advantage.

31
00:01:53,733 --> 00:01:58,189
This changes where the learning signal goes, while retaining the original sample level

32
00:01:58,189 --> 00:01:58,500
scale.

33
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:02,088
The calibrated rewards define group relative advantages.

34
00:02:02,088 --> 00:02:06,243
Runtime adjusted token advantages then enter the clipped GRPO objective, alongside KL

35
00:02:06,243 --> 00:02:10,202
regularization. Experience grounding, visual calibration, and precise attribution

36
00:02:10,202 --> 00:02:12,500
operate together in a single optimization loop.

37
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:17,909
After forty training steps and six hundred and forty processed requests, Mini Games

38
00:02:17,909 --> 00:02:22,029
total score rises from sixty eight point eight to seventy five point three.

39
00:02:22,029 --> 00:02:26,644
WebGen Bench accuracy improves from forty eight point eight to fifty six point nine,

40
00:02:26,644 --> 00:02:29,500
demonstrating transfer beyond game focused training.

41
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,982
The training dynamics reveal why all three components matter.

42
00:02:33,982 --> 00:02:39,162
With only the GUI assessor, webpage accuracy and game functionality improve, while game

43
00:02:39,162 --> 00:02:44,401
aesthetics fall sharply. Using the paper baseline, aesthetics drop from eighty one point

44
00:02:44,401 --> 00:02:46,307
five to seventy one point three.

45
00:02:46,307 --> 00:02:51,070
Better local task performance can therefore conceal deterioration in the overall

46
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:52,320
interactive artifact.

47
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:58,193
Self anchoring helps early, but its webpage accuracy later declines from fifty six point

48
00:02:58,193 --> 00:03:02,540
four to forty six point seven. A stronger reference better preserves late stage

49
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,411
performance, despite fluctuations.

50
00:03:04,411 --> 00:03:09,253
The conclusion is not that any reference is sufficient: reference quality determines how

51
00:03:09,253 --> 00:03:12,500
reliably visual calibration constrains reward exploitation.

52
00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:18,040
Action Trace Credit reaches fifty six point eight percent WebGen accuracy at step

53
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,731
thirty. The same strong anchor without it reaches that threshold at step seventy:

54
00:03:22,731 --> 00:03:27,421
roughly two point three times fewer training steps to the same observed accuracy.

55
00:03:27,421 --> 00:03:29,795
Functional testing also improves earlier.

56
00:03:29,795 --> 00:03:34,370
This is a checkpoint efficiency comparison, not a claim about wall clock speed.

57
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:41,500
Now, live comparisons: original Qwen on the left, Web Catalyst on the right.

58
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:44,321
A three dimensional flight game.

59
00:03:44,321 --> 00:03:47,954
In this example, the original remains on its launch screen.

60
00:03:47,954 --> 00:03:53,003
Web Catalyst produces an active flight scene, with responsive lane changes, moving

61
00:03:53,003 --> 00:03:56,390
obstacles, and continuously updated distance and score.

62
00:03:58,350 --> 00:04:01,376
A deck building adventure tests linked transitions.

63
00:04:01,376 --> 00:04:04,283
Select a route, play cards, and advance the turn.

64
00:04:04,283 --> 00:04:09,326
Watch energy consumption, enemy health, and the feedback that connects each action to

65
00:04:09,326 --> 00:04:10,750
the evolving game state.

66
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,731
The same principle extends beyond games.

67
00:04:16,731 --> 00:04:21,492
Add a habit, mark it complete, and see the statistics and three dimensional tree

68
00:04:21,492 --> 00:04:26,670
respond. Functionality and visual richness are part of the same interactive experience.

69
00:04:30,350 --> 00:04:33,603
Twenty four prompts, forty eight interactive artifacts.

70
00:04:33,603 --> 00:04:38,275
Each pair shows the same request: original Qwen in blue, Web Catalyst in green.

71
00:04:38,275 --> 00:04:43,243
These parallel recordings reveal the breadth of the generated experiences, while the

72
00:04:43,243 --> 00:04:46,910
benchmarks and training curves provide the aggregate evidence.

73
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:57,656
Web Catalyst. High fidelity experience, calibrated rewards, and runtime grounded credit:

74
00:04:57,656 --> 00:05:00,450
catalyzing interactive HTML generation.